-- title:
--   Completed local ring at an ordinary point is normal
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, naturals $\ell_g, M'$ with $\ell_g$ prime, $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, $M' \neq 0$, $q \nmid M'$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$ and whose residue field is finite, and in which $\ell_g$ and $M'$ are units. Assume: `hℓ`, that for every $A_0$-algebra $T$, Weierstrass curve $W/T$, variable change $C$ and level-$p$ datum $D = (x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$, the conditions "$(x_P,y_P)$ lies on the affine curve, $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{\ell_g}(x_P)=0$, $x_Q=x_P$, $y_Q=y_P$" are preserved by $C$; `hM`, that the $\Gamma_0(p^k)$-kernel condition `IsGamma0PowAt` (the two-torsion condition `IsTwoKernel` when $p^k=2$, otherwise the cyclic-kernel conditions on degree, leading coefficient, divisibility of $\mathrm{pre}\Psi$ and of the $a$-multiplication numerators) is preserved by `kernelVariableChangeDeg`; `hL`, that divisibility of `inLineMulPoly` is likewise preserved. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a family of relative group laws on the projective models of curves with unit discriminant, chord–tangent and with identity the origin section, and $\mathcal{T}$ a compatible level-$q$ transport of raw Drinfeld pairs; assume the existence of graded homomorphisms on the projective models realising variable changes (`hVC`) and coefficient changes (`hCO`). Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package, of finite type over $A_0$, for the moduli datum of `rigidDataH1Pow A₀ ℓg M' q hℓ hM hL 𝒢 𝒯`, with coefficient ring $B_0 =$ `P₀.B₀` and universal point `P₀.univ`; let $x$ be a raw object over $B_0$ (a Weierstrass curve of unit discriminant with $\Gamma_0$-polynomials indexed by the prime factors of $M'$, a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point, a Drinfeld basis of level $q$, and the linking divisibility) whose class is `P₀.univ`. Let $\mathfrak{m} \subset B_0$ be a maximal ideal containing the image of $q$, and $F_0$ a formal group over $B_0/\mathfrak{m}$ whose power series is the fixed formal group law of $x$.`curve` reduced mod $\mathfrak{m}$, and suppose $F_0$ is ordinary in the sense that its $q$-series (defined by $[0]=0$, $[n+1](X)=F_0([n](X),X)$) equals $u \cdot X^q$ for a unit $u$. Then the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of $B_0$ is a domain, is integrally closed, and the image of $q$ in it is nonzero.
--
--   This is the statement that the completed local ring of the fine moduli ring of the $H_1$-type level structure at an ordinary closed point of the fibre above $q$ is an integrally closed domain of mixed characteristic, in the style of the local structure theory of Katz–Mazur at ordinary points. It feeds the results on flatness and integral closedness of quotients by minimal primes and on the identification of the completion modulo the $q$-adic filtration at such points.
